!data/sample_data.txt

# Generated train/val/test splits (standard output location of the
# preprocessing scripts/config defaults) and large raw corpora - these can
# be 100MB+ and must never be committed (GitHub hard-blocks files >100MB).
data/train.tsv
data/val.tsv
data/test.tsv
data/quick_train.tsv

# Source translation memories, and anything derived straight from them.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. The Church TMX data is licensed course material,
# not ours to publish, and one of the files supplied is named "Sensitive". It
# also runs to gigabytes per file, well past GitHub's hard 100MB block, so a
# single `git add -A` would create a commit that cannot be pushed and cannot be
# undone without rewriting history.
#
# Keep the raw data outside git entirely, along with anything derived straight
# from it. Extraction, cleaning and the raw corpora live in the private sibling
# repository `torchlingo-private`, which also explains why.
*.tmx
*.tmx.gz
German/
German.zip

# Derived corpora at the top of `data/`, allowlisted rather than named one by
# one. The previous rules listed `train.tsv`, `val.tsv`, `test.tsv` and
# `quick_train.tsv` individually, so a corpus under any other name was staged by
# `git add -A` without complaint. Ignore the pattern and name the exceptions.
#
# `data/pretrained/` and `data/multilingual_example/` are untouched by this,
# since the pattern is not recursive.
data/*.tsv
!data/example.tsv

# Litter from executing a notebook in place.
#
# The tutorials write `data/` and `checkpoints/` relative to their own location,
# which is why `scripts/execute_notebooks.py` runs them in a scratch directory.
# Run nbconvert by hand instead and they land here. `checkpoints/` above already
# matches at any depth, but `data/train.tsv` contains a slash and so anchors to
# the repository root, which is how a stray `docs/docs/tutorials/data/train.tsv`
# got past it.
docs/docs/tutorials/data/
docs/docs/tutorials/checkpoints/

# Checkpoints and outputs
checkpoints/
*.pt
outputs/*.txt
outputs/*.log

# ...except the tutorial's pretrained model, which is committed on purpose.
# A tutorial that must train a model before it can show anything is a tutorial
# nobody finishes, and the whole point of this one is seeing real translations
# immediately. Regenerate with scripts/train_example_model.py.
!data/pretrained/model.pt

# TensorBoard
runs/
slurm/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.log

# Data - keep example files, ignore everything else
!data/example.tsv
!data/example_en_subset.txt
!data/example_es_subset.txt

docs/site/
docs/.cache/

# mkdocs-jupyter caches relative to the working directory, so building with
# `--config-file docs/mkdocs.yml` from the repo root (which CI does) writes
# here rather than under docs/.
.cache/
attention_alignment.png

